IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g7-fourth-schedule`
IMPORT `g7-commencement`
IMPORT `g7-electrical`
IMPORT `g7-regulations`

-- ind-b-tests-g7.l4: INDEPENDENT tests (author ind-b) of ss.58 to 63 and the Fourth Schedule.
-- Every expected value comes from work/ind-b/expectations.md, written from the sources BEFORE the encoding
-- was opened; the scenario id of that file is given beside each assertion.  Nothing here was edited to match
-- the code.  Failing assertions live in ind-b-tests-disagree.l4 and ind-b-tests-ambiguous.l4, not here.

§ `ind-b: independent tests of sections 58 to 63 and the Fourth Schedule`

§§ `Fixtures`

-- The actual facts: the Law published in Sefer HaChukim 3349 on 14.1.2025 (cover and page footers of the
-- gazette); the Fees Regulations published 9.7.2025 (Kovetz HaTakanot 11951), in force 7 days later (reg.5),
-- 16.7.2025; no regulations under s.46 in the sources.
GIVEN s46 IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63`
`ind-b actual facts, with s.46 regulations` s46 MEANS
    `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63` WITH
        `the day the Law was published in Reshumot` IS YMD 2025 1 14
        `the s.59 regulations came into force on` IS YMD 2025 7 16
        `the day regulations under section 46 came into force, if any` IS s46

GIVEN regs IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63`
`ind-b facts with the s.59 regulations in force on` regs MEANS
    `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63` WITH
        `the day the Law was published in Reshumot` IS YMD 2025 1 14
        `the s.59 regulations came into force on` IS regs
        `the day regulations under section 46 came into force, if any` IS NOTHING

GIVEN d IS A STRING, isLawful IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Cooling system`
`ind-b a 10 kW system using` d `lawful` isLawful MEANS
    `Cooling system` WITH
        `cooling capacity in kilowatts` IS 10
        `refrigerants` IS LIST (Refrigerant WITH `designation` IS d, `use of the refrigerant is permitted by law` IS isLawful)

GIVEN isApproved IS A BOOLEAN, isConsulted IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Procedure of the Minister's regulations`
`ind-b procedure, approved` isApproved `consulted` isConsulted MEANS
    `Procedure of the Minister's regulations` WITH
        `the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the regulations` IS isApproved
        `the Minister consulted the Minister concerned with the fields of the testers or experts` IS isConsulted

§§ `Fourth Schedule: every item, by number and designation as the gazette prints it (S4-1..95)`

-- Pairs scripted from inputs/law.wiki by work/ind-b/scripts/sched4.py; item (66) carries the gazette's E170
-- (printed page 207, image and text layer), not the wiki's 170E; direction marks stripped.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-b the Schedule has item` n `as` d MEANS
    any (GIVEN i YIELD i's `number of the item` EQUALS n AND i's `designation` EQUALS d) `the Fourth Schedule`

