§§ `s.63: dates on which readings A and B agree (K63-5, 8, 13, 14, 17, 21)`

-- K63-17: regulations in force 1.1.2025, before publication: both readings give 14.4.2025 (IL s.10(b)), and
-- (a)(2) 18 months later, 14.10.2026.
#ASSERT `the commencement day under section 63(a)(1)` (`ind-b facts with the s.59 regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 1 1)) EQUALS YMD 2025 4 14
#ASSERT `the day the Law commences for a system with any other refrigerant under section 63(a)(2)` (`ind-b facts with the s.59 regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 1 1)) EQUALS YMD 2026 10 14
-- K63-21: regulations in force on the day of publication: 14.4.2025.
#ASSERT `the commencement day under section 63(a)(1)` (`ind-b facts with the s.59 regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 1 14)) EQUALS YMD 2025 4 14

-- K63-5: a lawful listed refrigerant (290), the day before the regulations came into force: not commenced.
#ASSERT NOT `the Law has commenced for work on the system` (`ind-b a 10 kW system using` "290" `lawful` TRUE) `on the day` (YMD 2025 7 15) `given the facts` (`ind-b actual facts, with s.46 regulations` NOTHING)
-- K63-8: 410A on 16.10.2025: not commenced under either reading.
#ASSERT NOT `the Law has commenced for work on the system` (`ind-b a 10 kW system using` "410A" `lawful` TRUE) `on the day` (YMD 2025 10 16) `given the facts` (`ind-b actual facts, with s.46 regulations` NOTHING)
-- K63-7 / K63-6 after both readings' (a)(2) day: 410A on 1.5.2027 has commenced.
#ASSERT `the Law has commenced for work on the system` (`ind-b a 10 kW system using` "410A" `lawful` TRUE) `on the day` (YMD 2027 5 1) `given the facts` (`ind-b actual facts, with s.46 regulations` NOTHING)
-- K63-2 under both readings: 290 on 16.10.2025 has commenced.
#ASSERT `the Law has commenced for work on the system` (`ind-b a 10 kW system using` "290" `lawful` TRUE) `on the day` (YMD 2025 10 16) `given the facts` (`ind-b actual facts, with s.46 regulations` NOTHING)
-- K63-9: a listed refrigerant whose use is NOT lawful (1270 assumed unlawful) falls under (a)(2):
-- on 1.6.2026, inside both readings' gap between (1) and (2), it has not commenced; a lawful 290 has.
#ASSERT `the regime of a system under section 63(a)` (`ind-b a 10 kW system using` "1270" `lawful` FALSE) EQUALS `the regime of paragraph (2)`
#ASSERT `the regime of a system under section 63(a)` (`ind-b a 10 kW system using` "290" `lawful` TRUE) EQUALS `the regime of paragraph (1)`
#ASSERT `the regime of a system under section 63(a)` (`ind-b a 10 kW system using` "410A" `lawful` TRUE) EQUALS `the regime of paragraph (2)`
#ASSERT `the regime of a system under section 63(a)` (`ind-b a 10 kW system using` "134a" `lawful` TRUE) EQUALS `the regime of paragraph (2)`
#ASSERT NOT `the Law has commenced for work on the system` (`ind-b a 10 kW system using` "1270" `lawful` FALSE) `on the day` (YMD 2026 6 1) `given the facts` (`ind-b actual facts, with s.46 regulations` NOTHING)
#ASSERT `the Law has commenced for work on the system` (`ind-b a 10 kW system using` "290" `lawful` TRUE) `on the day` (YMD 2026 6 1) `given the facts` (`ind-b actual facts, with s.46 regulations` NOTHING)

-- K63-13: s.46 regulations in force 1.1.2028, later than 18 months under either reading.
#ASSERT `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` (YMD 2028 1 1) `given the facts` (`ind-b actual facts, with s.46 regulations` (JUST (YMD 2028 1 1)))
#ASSERT NOT `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` (YMD 2027 12 31) `given the facts` (`ind-b actual facts, with s.46 regulations` (JUST (YMD 2028 1 1)))
#ASSERT NOT `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` (YMD 2027 6 1) `given the facts` (`ind-b actual facts, with s.46 regulations` (JUST (YMD 2028 1 1)))
#ASSERT `the day Chapter 6 commences under section 63(b)` (`ind-b actual facts, with s.46 regulations` (JUST (YMD 2028 1 1))) EQUALS YMD 2028 1 1
-- K63-14: s.46 regulations in force 16.4.2027: Chapter 6 commences 16.4.2027 under both readings.
#ASSERT `the day Chapter 6 commences under section 63(b)` (`ind-b actual facts, with s.46 regulations` (JUST (YMD 2027 4 16))) EQUALS YMD 2027 4 16

§§ `s.63: reading B (the later of three months from publication and the regulations' day), as the encoder took it`

-- These are the Reading B column of expectations.md, which I wrote as the alternative; they pass because the
-- encoder took B.  Reading A is asserted, and fails, in ind-b-tests-ambiguous.l4.
#ASSERT `s 63(a)(1) — the commencement day, under the readings` (`ind-b actual facts, with s.46 regulations` NOTHING) `the readings of the dates taken` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16
#ASSERT `s 63(a)(2) — the day the Law commences for a system with any other refrigerant, under the readings` (`ind-b actual facts, with s.46 regulations` NOTHING) `the readings of the dates taken` EQUALS YMD 2027 1 16
#ASSERT `the commencement day under section 63(a)(1)` (`ind-b facts with the s.59 regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 3 1)) EQUALS YMD 2025 4 14
#ASSERT `the commencement day under section 63(a)(1)` (`ind-b facts with the s.59 regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 4 14)) EQUALS YMD 2025 4 14
#ASSERT `the commencement day under section 63(a)(1)` (`ind-b facts with the s.59 regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 11 30)) EQUALS YMD 2025 11 30

-- Reading A is available as the encoder's alternative record; with it, my Reading A column holds.
#ASSERT `s 63(a)(1) — the commencement day, under the readings` (`ind-b actual facts, with s.46 regulations` NOTHING) `the readings of the dates with the three months counted from the later of the two days` EQUALS YMD 2025 10 16
#ASSERT `s 63(a)(2) — the day the Law commences for a system with any other refrigerant, under the readings` (`ind-b actual facts, with s.46 regulations` NOTHING) `the readings of the dates with the three months counted from the later of the two days` EQUALS YMD 2027 4 16
#ASSERT `s 63(a)(1) — the commencement day, under the readings` (`ind-b facts with the s.59 regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 3 1)) `the readings of the dates with the three months counted from the later of the two days` EQUALS YMD 2025 6 1
#ASSERT `s 63(a)(1) — the commencement day, under the readings` (`ind-b facts with the s.59 regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 4 14)) `the readings of the dates with the three months counted from the later of the two days` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 14
#ASSERT `s 63(a)(1) — the commencement day, under the readings` (`ind-b facts with the s.59 regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 11 30)) `the readings of the dates with the three months counted from the later of the two days` EQUALS YMD 2026 2 28
#ASSERT `s 63(a)(2) — the day the Law commences for a system with any other refrigerant, under the readings` (`ind-b facts with the s.59 regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 11 30)) `the readings of the dates with the three months counted from the later of the two days` EQUALS YMD 2027 8 28
#ASSERT `s 63(a)(2) — the day the Law commences for a system with any other refrigerant, under the readings` (`ind-b facts with the s.59 regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 3 1)) `the readings of the dates with the three months counted from the later of the two days` EQUALS YMD 2026 12 1
#ASSERT `s 63(a)(2) — the day the Law commences for a system with any other refrigerant, under the readings` (`ind-b facts with the s.59 regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 4 14)) `the readings of the dates with the three months counted from the later of the two days` EQUALS YMD 2027 1 14

-- K63-12 under Reading A, through the encoder's alternative record: Chapter 6 commences 16.4.2027.
#ASSERT `s 63(b) — the day Chapter 6 commences, under the readings` (`ind-b actual facts, with s.46 regulations` (JUST (YMD 2026 1 1))) `the readings of the dates with the three months counted from the later of the two days` EQUALS YMD 2027 4 16
-- K63-11, my answer (no s.46 regulations: not commenced), through the encoder's alternative of fork F-C-8.
#ASSERT NOT `s 63(b) — reading no regulation under section 46 as none in force, Chapter 6 has commenced on the day` (YMD 2030 1 1) (`ind-b actual facts, with s.46 regulations` NOTHING) `the readings of the dates taken`

§§ `s.63: rest days do not move a commencement (K63-10, K63-16)`

-- The fleet default (kind C, no IL s.10(c)), which I share: a rest day on the day does not move it.  Supplied
-- through the reading record that carries a calendar but does not apply s.10(c).
GIVETH A `Readings of the dates of section 63`
`ind-b readings taken, with a calendar naming 16.10.2025, 16.1.2027 and 16.4.2027` MEANS
    `Readings of the dates of section 63` WITH
        `IL s.10(c) is applied to a period counted from another date` IS FALSE
        `the Law commences on the day after a period of months ends` IS FALSE
        `the three months of paragraph (1) run from the later of the two days` IS FALSE
        `the calendar of rest days` IS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST YMD 2025 10 16, YMD 2027 1 16, YMD 2027 4 16

#ASSERT `s 63(a)(2) — the day the Law commences for a system with any other refrigerant, under the readings` (`ind-b actual facts, with s.46 regulations` NOTHING) `ind-b readings taken, with a calendar naming 16.10.2025, 16.1.2027 and 16.4.2027` EQUALS YMD 2027 1 16
#ASSERT `s 63(b) — the day 18 months from the commencement day, under the readings` (`ind-b actual facts, with s.46 regulations` NOTHING) `ind-b readings taken, with a calendar naming 16.10.2025, 16.1.2027 and 16.4.2027` EQUALS YMD 2027 1 16

§§ `s.63: the provisions that are not about work on a system`

-- expectations.md, "Unanswered by the source": s.63(a) fixes a commencement only "for the performance of work on
-- a system"; for the Registrar, the Council and inspection it gives no day.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the Law has commenced, for a provision that is not about work on a system, on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1)

